course: dictionary
lesson: 1506
title: Celebration and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Celebration» is a good example. Its first meaning is a special event, like a party. Its second meaning is showing that you are happy about something.
explain: Read the words around the word first. «Gunpowder was used for celebrations long before it was used in guns.» Here celebrations means special events, such as parties and festivals, because people used gunpowder for them.
explain: Sometimes the clue is a phrase. «A cause for celebration» means a good reason to be happy and have a party. «In celebration of» means to show that you are happy about something. When you meet a phrase you don't know, try swapping in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A celebration is a special event, like a party, held because something good has happened or for a special day.
fact: Celebration can also mean the act of showing that you are happy about something.
fact: Formal writing sometimes uses celebration for a religious ceremony.
fact: «A cause for celebration» means a good reason to be happy.
fact: «Mnohaya lita» means "many years", and it is a song sung at birthdays and celebrations.
fact: The Māori haka is used for welcomes, celebrations, funerals and challenges.
exercise: Mum said, «Let's have a celebration for your good report!» What is a celebration? | A kind of school lesson | A quiet walk alone | *A special event to mark something good | A tiring chore to do before bed
exercise: «The whole village came to the birthday celebrations, with music and cake.» What are the celebrations? | Lessons about maths | *Happy parties and special events | Long, boring meetings | Rainy-day walks
exercise: Dad said, «Winning the match is a cause for celebration!» What does cause for celebration mean? | A bad sign for the team | *A good reason to be happy and have a party | A reason to be cross | A rule about football
test: «Her friends made a celebration of her first day at the new school.» What does celebration show? | That they were angry | *That they were happy and wanted to mark the day | That she had lost something | That the school was closed
test: «The church held a special celebration on Sunday.» What does celebration mean here? | A long sleep | *A formal religious ceremony | A shopping trip | A school test
exam: The song «mnohaya lita» means "many years". Where is it sung? | Only at bedtime | In a maths lesson | On a rainy walk | *At birthdays and celebrations
